# res://dialogue/layla_runs_away.dialogue
# step 2.323: TEMPLATE test scene for the memory box chapter "Layla Runs Away", to see Fiona and Layla
# against a room. plays in place over the hub through conversation/layla_runs_away_overlay.tscn, after
# the portal swirl and the "layla_runs_away" monologue in dialogue/chapter_launch.dialogue.
# rooms: the overlay's background aliases ("apt_living_room", "apt_living_room_2", in
# res://Backgrounds/Apartment/ since step 2.413).
# step 2.330: the coffee is a closer, blurred view of the same room (background_view) with the overlay's
# "table" foreground in front (Backgrounds/Apartment/fiona_apartment_coffee_table.png).
# step 2.324: Layla uses only her "base" sprite (the one from the puzzle level). her other expressions
# in characters/layla_profile.tres are old art and are not to be used.
# step 2.326: the same afternoon as the car ride. they come in through the front door on the left, at an
# easy pace (actor_stroll_in / actor_stroll_to / actor_stroll_out; the dialogue waits while they walk).
# step 2.328: facing. both sprites face right unflipped (flip = face left).
#   Fiona walks in facing the room, turns back to the door (flipped) and backs up to make room;
#   Layla walks in facing the room, glances back at the door (flipped), then turns to Fiona (unflipped).
# then a cut to the two of them on the sofa (actor_sit), Layla on the left, Fiona on the right facing her.
# test on its own: Dev/layla_runs_away_test.tscn (F6).

~ start
# already staged when it comes from the memory box; needed when the scene is run on its own
do change_background("apt_living_room", "none", 0.0)
# step 2.410: her mischief theme, from the arrival until the pose (a record stop cuts it there)
do SoundManager.play_music_track("mischief_music", 2.0)
A few minutes and a climb of stairs later, you arrive at your apartment.
# step 2.339: the door unlocks - the dialogue waits for the sound to finish - then Fiona walks in
do SoundManager.play_sfx_and_wait("door_unlock")
# step 2.327: she stops just inside, about one of her own widths from the left edge
do actor_stroll_in("Fiona", "base", "0.3", 2.2)
# she looks back over her shoulder at the door...
do actor_flip("Fiona", true)
Player: Come on in.
# ...and backs up into the room to make way, still facing the door
do actor_stroll_to("Fiona", "0.6", 1.6)
# step 2.344: Layla comes in to about where Fiona stopped...
# step 2.365: she comes in curious, looking around
do actor_stroll_in("Layla", "curious", "0.28", 2.4)
# ...glances back at the door and the plant...
do actor_flip("Layla", true)
do wait(0.7)
do actor_flip("Layla", false)
# ...and wanders on across the room, looking around, passing in front of Fiona to the far side
do actor_stroll_to("Layla", "0.84", 3.2)
# step 2.345: at the far side she turns and wanders back, past Fiona again, to Fiona's left, then turns
# to face her (Fiona is still facing the door side, so she already faces Layla)
do actor_flip("Layla", true)
do wait(0.4)
do actor_stroll_to("Layla", "0.33", 2.6)
do actor_flip("Layla", false)
# step 2.366: an open mouth when she speaks, the same mood with her mouth closed while Fiona does
do actor_change("Layla", "excited")
Layla: Fiona! This apartment is huge!
do actor_change("Layla", "explaining_talk")
Layla: And so neat and tidy! I love it.
do actor_change("Layla", "explaining")
Player: Thanks.
do actor_change("Layla", "asking")
Layla: Are your roommates home right now?
do actor_change("Layla", "curious")
do actor_change("Fiona", "hands_back")
Player: I don't have any.
Player: I've been living alone for a while now.
do actor_change("Layla", "pensive")
Layla takes a second to process that.
# step 2.367/2.368: genuinely impressed (not blushing) - how can a grad student afford this?
do actor_change("Layla", "wowed")
do actor_effect("Layla", "bounce")
